{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Gerrit **1400** pushed — test-only, and the probe turned out to be unnecessary\n\nStacked on **1399** (9f26). One file: `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py`, no\nproduction code.\n\n### What changed in the cell\n\n`test_outbound_clear_parent_round_trips` now clears an **Epic Link on a standard-issue child**\ninstead of `fields.parent` on a sub-task. This ticket's own analysis of the managed-ref gate was\n**correct and is load-bearing**: `_parent_clear_is_managed` -> `should_propagate_removal` fires\nonly for a ref in `managed_refs`, and `reducer/_processors.py:528` folds it in on a local\n`edit_ticket(..., parent=...)`. So the cell primes the parent through a LOCAL rebar edit carried\nby a real pass — not by creating the issue under a parent Jira-side, which is what the old cell\ndid and what left the ref unmanaged.\n\nAssertion count went **7 -> 10**. No skip, no xfail, no loosened round trip.\n\n### A vacuous-green bug in my own first draft, caught in review\n\nMy first version ended with `assert not after` on the Epic Link **without checking the HTTP\nstatus**. A 401/403/500 returns a dict like `{\"errorMessages\": [...]}`, whose `.get(\"fields\")`\nis None — so `after` was falsy and **the cell would have gone GREEN on a failed read**. Now\nasserts `status == 200 and isinstance(body, dict) and \"fields\" in body` first. The positive\nassertions above it (comparing against an expected key) are safe without that; a\n**must-be-absent** oracle never is. Worth generalising: every \"assert X is gone\" oracle in this\nsuite needs the read proven successful first.\n\n### The probe: keep it, but the question it was built for is settled\n\n`scripts/jira_dc_epic_link_clear_probe.py` and its workflow are untouched and still land. But two\ngreen cells in run 30951453979 already answered its question, so it was not on the critical path.\nThe R2 finding it produced — **`serverInfo` 200 is NOT readiness for Jira Software custom\nfields** — stands on its own and is a latent hazard for any new workflow using that gate.\n\n### AC status\n\n- [x] the probe's verdict question — **ANSWERED: it clears** (via the harness, not the probe)\n- [ ] the re-home is written and lints clean; **needs a live run to confirm green** (run id to be\n      recorded here)\n- [n/a] the \"if it does NOT clear\" branch — not triggered\n- [superseded] the `xfail(strict=True)` AC — the operator ruling on [rebar:9f26-66c2-14af-4223]\n      forbids xfail; that cell is re-homed under 9f26 instead\n- [x] no cell weakened\n\nGates: `make lint` **0**, `make typecheck` **0**, marker-selected suite **0** (10202 passed).\n**Not closing** — needs the harness run."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785889876399259001,"uuid":"d3750c8d-0dbf-492e-9d83-64ade33c3937"}